\f1\fs22 \
\
South from  Jamison Valley and spread above Sublime Point, thousands of points holding station at differing depths until the sky looked less occupied than infested.\
\
\
Kylie Minogue occupied a broad section of the east while Chris Hemsworth emerged farther west, requiring so many drones around the jaw that Con the Fruiterer had to form underneath him. Margot Robbie appeared beside Kylie. Bert Newton smiled down over a UDF checkpoint. Steve Irwin materialised over an artillery position, sharing the southern edge of the display with a prime minister drinking a yardglass of pissy Oxford ale in eleven seconds.\
The Elvi applauded.\
Several UDF troops did too.\
Then every face disappeared at once.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf2 TAMPERING WITH STASIS TECHNOLOGY MAY INVALIDATE THE WARRANTY OF YOUR LIFE
\f1\b0 \
The warning remained long enough for everybody who needed reminding to be reminded.\
Then the swarm rearranged itself.\

\f2\b LAY DOWN YOUR ARMS
\f1\b0 \
A second line formed underneath.\

\f2\b COOPERATE
\f1\b0 \
Then:\

\f2\b SURRENDER
\f1\b0 \
The last word had barely settled when small areas of the display began going dark.\
Five lights vanished near the first 
\f3\i R
\f1\i0 .\
Five disappeared from the bottom of the 
\f3\i S
\f1\i0 .\
Another five came out of the space between the words.\
The illuminated drones moved fractionally closer together and repaired the message.\
The darkened pentads came down.\
The first group selected a UDF anti-aircraft vehicle south of Willoughby Road.\
One drone took position above it. Four distributed themselves around it in a geometry which, from ground level, looked almost casual. None pointed at the vehicle. None fired.\
Small circular housings beneath them opened.\
Five Gyges discs spun.\
The vehicle started shaking.\
The men beside it did not.\
Neither did the road three metres away, the scrub behind it, nor the folding table on which somebody had left a mug of coffee.\
The vehicle shook harder.\
Its radar dish departed first, followed by two access panels and a piece of equipment which had cost the Ulyssian taxpayer enough to make the procurement officer responsible for it briefly famous in an internal audit.\
The coffee remained on the table.\
Then the five drones separated.\
Before the anti-aircraft vehicle had finished destroying itself, the pentad was moving towards something else.\
That was when the UDF began to understand the fives.\
A pentad settled around an artillery emplacement.\
The gun crew abandoned it.\
The gun began to shake.\
Not the ammunition stacked six metres away. Not the men diving for the roadside. The gun.\
Its mounting failed.\
Another five surrounded a communications vehicle.\
Another arranged itself around the forward checkpoint.\
Another dropped low around an armoured carrier wedged between two other vehicles on Sublime Point Road.\
The UDF had deployed sensibly for the geography. Equipment was distributed along the narrow road, infantry pushed out towards the bush, command and communications farther north, heavier equipment spaced wherever the road permitted.\
Fridge Force attacked the arrangement one useful noun at a time.\
Gun.\
Radar.\
Carrier.\
Communications.\
Checkpoint.\
Everywhere five drones settled, something began experiencing a private earthquake.\
The machines were MoSES.\
Mobile Stasis Energy Systems.\
A popular anti-social-network claim maintained that MoSES technology could chill an esky of micro-brewed ale in 42^42 Planck times.\
Nobody at Sublime Point had an esky of micro-brewed ale available for independent verification.\
The UDF fired back.\
MoSES pentads broke apart before missiles could acquire them, crossed through the larger swarm, and formed around new targets. Other drones kept the sky full of light and noise. Five dark machines might vanish into several hundred illuminated ones, then reappear fifty metres away already arranging themselves around something the UDF had been hoping to continue owning.\
Some pentads crossed towards the Shakti compound.\
Those had a shorter life expectancy.\
The first five crossed the perimeter and ceased to exist.\
There was no explosion. One instant five machines were flying; the next there were several twists of black smoke and five brief rainbow flashes falling through the air.\
The Gyges discs survived.\
Another pentad came in lower.\
Three drones disappeared. The other two broke away.\
A third crossed between the auditorium and the hover-copt pad.\
It vanished in sections.\
Eloise had never been modest about the quality of the above-ground defences at Sublime Point. Whatever Fridge Force knew about stasis, Shakti Enterprises remained extremely competent at making airborne objects stop being airborne objects.\
But there were a great many drones.\
Two complete pentads made it through.\
They passed the Shakti residence, dropped over the functional part of the compound, crossed between the auditorium and the hover-copt pad and headed for the Ruined Castle access.\
Nobody outside followed them.\
There was quite enough happening outside already.\
A pentad had started forming around the Elvi stage.\
\'93Five!\'94\
Elvi who had spent the previous several minutes watching UDF equipment discover the number's tactical significance arrived at the same conclusion.\
They scattered.\
Five drones widened around the stage.\
One crossed behind the amplifiers. Two spread either side. Another climbed.\
An Elvis reached into an open guitar case and pulled out a Gyges disc.\
The cases had proved useful for getting the discs through UDF checkpoints. This was the first indication that they might also be useful for getting them back out.\
He threw it.\
The disc missed every drone.\
It passed through the space between them.\
The pentad moved.\
One drone rose sharply. Two corrected sideways. The other pair shifted to restore whatever relationship had just been disturbed.\
For a moment all five Gyges discs under the drones changed pitch.\
Nothing happened to the stage.\
The Elvi watched.\
Another guitar case opened.\
The next disc went through the pentad from the other direction.\
Again the drones moved to compensate.\
Again nothing shook.\
Several hundred Elvi reached the same scientific conclusion at roughly the same time.\
They began throwing things physicists had spent most of the novel trying not to touch.\
The next pentad received four Gyges discs.\
One went over it.\
One went under.\
One struck the bonnet of a Continental and ricocheted through the formation.\
The fourth passed between two MoSES drones closely enough for the rainbow interference around both discs to flare white.\
The five drones scattered.\
The Elvi cheered.\
They did not waste time discussing it.\
Guitar cases opened all along the road.\
The UDF had rifles, artillery and counter-drone systems.\
The Elvi had stolen spacetime components and very little respect for throwing technique.\
It was enough.\
MoSES pentads trying to settle around the Elvi found loose Gyges discs passing through the spaces their own discs required them to maintain. Some broke formation early. Others attempted corrections until the geometry collapsed. One drone moved sideways out of a formation, clipped a lighting gantry and fell through the roof of a white Lincoln Continental.\
Its owner stared at the hole.\
\'93Tax.\'94\
The disc survived.\
Someone retrieved it.\
At the gate, the stage was already assembled.\
The Elvi had been there long enough to possess the kind of amplification normally associated with an international tour, an unstable government or a neighbour dispute involving several farms.\
Someone turned the speakers towards Sublime Point.\
Someone else called for 
\f3\i You\'92ll Never Walk Alone
\f1\i0 .\
The choice spread faster than any order could have.\
The opening came out of the amplifiers almost recognisably.\
By the time the Elvi joined it, the song had acquired several hundred additional voices, multiple guitars, an upright bass and enough low-frequency reinforcement to give the gate a personal interest in the performance.\
The UDF heard it too.\
Somewhere near the forward positions, a soldier lowered his rifle.\
Another did the same.\
A third started crying.\
This turned out to be contagious.\
The gates were less sentimental.\
They remained closed.\
The Elvi sang louder.\
Shakti security had been built to recognise threats. Gunfire was a threat. Explosives were a threat. Unauthorised vehicles, anomalous heat, broken glass and people attempting to climb things Eloise had paid specifically to prevent them climbing were threats.\
Several hundred Elvi singing an Elvis-recorded Rodgers and Hammerstein song at military volume was still working its way through classification.\
The vibration sensors got there first.\
The gate began reporting movement without reporting an impact.\
The locking system disagreed with the structural monitors.\
The structural monitors disagreed with the acoustic system.\
The acoustic system had long since ceased contributing anything useful.\
The Elvi kept singing.\
The gate opened.\
The first Elvi through were the ones who had been leaning on it.\
Others followed on foot and in cars, still carrying guitar cases, weapons and whatever part of the band had not been plugged permanently into the road.\
The UDF did not follow.\
The UDF had MoSES.\
A pentad dropped around one of its remaining weapons positions.\
Another formed at the checkpoint.\
Farther north, five drones began distributing themselves around the command equipment.\
The UDF had reached the stage of the engagement where every intact piece of expensive machinery represented an invitation.\
Below Sublime Point, the two surviving pentads entered the Traverse.\
The tunnel ran for several kilometres through the mountain to Ruined Castle. It had been designed around service carts, equipment movements and the kind of private infrastructure that ceased sounding extravagant once somebody had already paid for it.\
The drones flew at about the speed of a golf cart driven by somebody who did not own the golf cart.\
They encountered little resistance.\
The serious defences were above them.\
A security door closed across the Traverse.\
The leading pentad slowed.\
Five drones spread around the section of tunnel containing it.\
Five Gyges discs spun.\
The door, frame and a carefully bounded quantity of surrounding rock began shaking.\
The tunnel immediately beyond them did not.\
The frame came away first.\
The door remained impressively locked while ceasing to have anything useful to be locked to.\
The pentads continued.\
Above them, UDF positions were still being reduced according to the number five. Outside the gate, Elvi were still throwing stolen Gyges discs into MoSES formations. Inside the compound, 
\f3\i You\'92ll Never Walk Alone
\f1\i0  continued moving south in several mutually incompatible keys.\
The two pentads reached Ruined Castle.\
They separated.\
Five went looking for Eloise Shakti.\
Five went looking for Project Kebab.\
The second group found the apparatus first.\
Johnny was still at it.\
Chip was still trying to stop him.\
Five drones entered the chamber and spread around the machinery.\
Their Gyges discs began to spin.\
Elsewhere in Ruined Castle, Sarah had found Eloise.\
She had walked out on Johnny and Chip to do it.\
The other pentad found them.\
One drone moved past Sarah. Another crossed behind Eloise. Three more spread until the five enclosed the space around her.\
Their discs spun up.\
The geometry tightened.\
And that's when Sarah's waters broke.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

